1
00:00:11,360 --> 00:00:17,540
Aiming for the setting sun
floating over the Nakagawa,

2
00:00:17,540 --> 00:00:24,660
I kicked a pebble and my shoes flew off too.

3
00:00:24,660 --> 00:00:32,900
Onto the head of the
carpenter who was chopping away,

4
00:00:32,900 --> 00:00:39,120
they laughed that I'm still just a kid.

5
00:00:39,940 --> 00:00:44,220
Even if I try somehow to lift my spirits,

6
00:00:44,220 --> 00:00:49,280
alone in Kameari,
with a yawn, nothing changes.

7
00:00:49,280 --> 00:00:53,160
The streets feel strangely gentle.

8
00:00:54,660 --> 00:01:01,140
From the pointed hat, from the water pot,

9
00:01:01,660 --> 00:01:07,460
the sun sinks into the vast sky.

10
00:01:11,240 --> 00:01:15,920
Tomorrow too,
it'll end just like this, won't it.

11
00:01:15,920 --> 00:01:19,740
Katsushika, Shibamata, happiness, they say.

12
00:01:19,740 --> 00:01:24,540
I'm a fool who only realized it too late.

13
00:01:29,220 --> 00:01:31,240
A beautiful wife is super intense!

14
00:01:48,820 --> 00:01:50,120
What do you think you're doing?

15
00:01:50,120 --> 00:01:55,600
Chief, you were here?

16
00:01:55,600 --> 00:01:57,580
You're here awfully early today.

17
00:01:57,580 --> 00:01:59,660
Shut up!

18
00:02:01,660 --> 00:02:03,620
What's going on?
I'm counting on you, Ryotsu!

19
00:02:06,820 --> 00:02:07,620
W-what?

20
00:02:09,600 --> 00:02:13,560
Even though your subordinate was
working outside of office hours,

21
00:02:14,100 --> 00:02:18,420
you're going to pour barley tea on
my head just for dozing off a little?

22
00:02:20,080 --> 00:02:21,680
Well, I was just...

23
00:02:21,680 --> 00:02:25,340
Truly, I'm so lucky to
have such a good boss.

24
00:02:27,480 --> 00:02:29,720
Ryotsu, good work.

25
00:02:32,640 --> 00:02:36,140
Then would it be all right if I
take a nice long nap in the back?

26
00:02:37,220 --> 00:02:38,620
Thanks a lot.

27
00:02:40,280 --> 00:02:41,960
Chief, is that really all right?

28
00:02:42,140 --> 00:02:43,200
We're on duty, you know.

29
00:02:52,180 --> 00:02:53,440
Part-time job?

30
00:02:54,060 --> 00:02:57,090
All you do is keep a Porsche
parked in one spot all night,

31
00:02:57,140 --> 00:02:58,600
and you get paid.

32
00:02:59,280 --> 00:03:01,060
Is there really a job like that?

33
00:03:01,060 --> 00:03:05,480
The owner of this car transferred to Tokyo,

34
00:03:05,480 --> 00:03:08,660
but he's had a hard time
finding a monthly parking space.

35
00:03:09,420 --> 00:03:12,120
Parking is in short supply in Tokyo,
isn't it.

36
00:03:12,540 --> 00:03:16,340
He can use his company's lot during the day,
so that's fine,

37
00:03:16,340 --> 00:03:19,220
but at night it costs 350
yen for every 30 minutes.

38
00:03:19,220 --> 00:03:22,120
He has to use a paid lot.

39
00:03:22,640 --> 00:03:25,600
So leaving it overnight really adds up,
doesn't it.

40
00:03:26,400 --> 00:03:28,680
Yeah, I hear it comes to nearly 10,000 yen.

41
00:03:29,320 --> 00:03:31,560
So that's why you asked
your senior for the job.

42
00:03:32,620 --> 00:03:33,188
Right.

43
00:03:33,238 --> 00:03:36,640
If you just keep driving around the Metropolitan
Expressway Loop Line at the speed limit,

44
00:03:36,640 --> 00:03:39,020
the gas costs aren't that high either.

45
00:03:40,220 --> 00:03:40,998
I see.

46
00:03:41,048 --> 00:03:44,860
Even if you add the senior's part-time pay,
gas, and highway tolls,

47
00:03:44,860 --> 00:03:47,280
it still comes out cheaper than parking fees

48
00:03:47,740 --> 00:03:48,800
You've really thought this through.

49
00:03:48,800 --> 00:03:51,680
Yeah, but I'm dead tired from lack of sleep.

50
00:03:52,180 --> 00:03:53,000
It's only four o'clock.

51
00:03:54,540 --> 00:03:56,640
Nakagawa, I'm taking over the driving.

52
00:03:57,200 --> 00:03:58,320
Pull the car over.

53
00:03:58,740 --> 00:03:59,100
Yes.

54
00:04:04,120 --> 00:04:13,460
It's a Corvette.

55
00:04:13,940 --> 00:04:16,080
They've modified the engine quite a bit.

56
00:04:16,080 --> 00:04:17,540
The driver was a beauty.

57
00:04:17,540 --> 00:04:18,820
Let's follow it, Nakagawa.

58
00:04:19,700 --> 00:04:21,900
You say that kind of thing,
and yet it's a dream.

59
00:04:23,140 --> 00:04:23,980
Hurry up.

60
00:04:28,740 --> 00:04:31,020
It's a silver metallic Corvette.

61
00:04:35,140 --> 00:04:37,020
One yen for a Corvette spin.

62
00:04:37,020 --> 00:04:38,720
Hey there, cheerful!

63
00:04:39,640 --> 00:04:42,080
Driving with a beauty at dawn is nice,
isn't it.

64
00:04:42,080 --> 00:04:43,280
Can you hear me?

65
00:04:43,520 --> 00:04:44,480
Good morning.

66
00:04:44,480 --> 00:04:45,960
Good morning.

67
00:04:45,960 --> 00:04:47,120
What a lovely morning.

68
00:04:47,120 --> 00:04:48,500
That's funny.

69
00:04:48,500 --> 00:04:50,260
Today's the day we did it!

70
00:04:50,740 --> 00:04:52,520
Nakagawa, take over driving!

71
00:04:53,000 --> 00:04:53,980
We can jump over to that one!

72
00:04:54,180 --> 00:04:55,580
That's a bit reckless!

73
00:04:58,220 --> 00:04:59,580
Hey, what is it?

74
00:05:04,240 --> 00:05:06,760
What's going on?

75
00:05:06,810 --> 00:05:09,380
Is it a crime?

76
00:05:09,860 --> 00:05:12,300
What a reckless car. I can't let that slide!

77
00:05:16,460 --> 00:05:18,340
A helmet just fell off!

78
00:05:19,640 --> 00:05:21,240
Don't cut through there, Nakagawa!

79
00:05:31,100 --> 00:05:33,660
Damn patrol car, it finally gave up

80
00:05:36,820 --> 00:05:38,060
What's with that car?

81
00:05:45,360 --> 00:05:46,680
Let's track it down.

82
00:05:59,200 --> 00:06:01,020
We sure brought them to a stop.

83
00:06:01,400 --> 00:06:03,880
What a bold, daring drive.

84
00:06:05,640 --> 00:06:07,200
Step out of the car.

85
00:06:08,080 --> 00:06:08,600
What?

86
00:06:11,200 --> 00:06:14,340
You're a woman? Damn it, you had to butt in.

87
00:06:16,160 --> 00:06:16,560
You bastard!

88
00:06:17,540 --> 00:06:18,620
Finally caught up!

89
00:06:22,860 --> 00:06:24,453
Thank you for your cooperation.

90
00:06:24,503 --> 00:06:27,009
It's a '68 Corvette, isn't it?

91
00:06:27,059 --> 00:06:28,520
It's really cool.

92
00:06:29,200 --> 00:06:30,300
Let go of me!

93
00:06:30,520 --> 00:06:32,020
Hey, behave yourself!

94
00:06:33,960 --> 00:06:35,080
Shut up!

95
00:06:42,960 --> 00:06:44,060
Thank you for your hard work.

96
00:06:46,380 --> 00:06:48,600
I'm from the Katsushika station.

97
00:06:49,400 --> 00:06:53,200
This guy's a habitual offender
of serious traffic violations.

98
00:06:53,200 --> 00:06:56,040
I see. I'll leave the rest to you two.

99
00:06:56,040 --> 00:06:57,020
Yes, sir!

100
00:06:58,400 --> 00:07:02,100
Wow, but that's some amazing
driving technique you have.

101
00:07:02,980 --> 00:07:05,000
It's nothing special, really.

102
00:07:05,560 --> 00:07:07,080
Do you like American cars?

103
00:07:08,260 --> 00:07:11,440
I'm so busy with work that
I can only drive at night.

104
00:07:11,720 --> 00:07:12,814
I see.

105
00:07:12,864 --> 00:07:17,440
I thought you were driving around all
night because you had no parking space.

106
00:07:18,380 --> 00:07:20,980
No one does that. You're a funny one.

107
00:07:21,260 --> 00:07:24,020
Well, there is someone like that,
right here.

108
00:07:25,220 --> 00:07:27,540
Would you like to get some tea,
if you're free?

109
00:07:30,320 --> 00:07:31,540
What should I do?

110
00:07:32,500 --> 00:07:35,900
You seem like fun,
so I'll keep you company until sunrise.

111
00:07:36,260 --> 00:07:37,120
Yes!

112
00:07:38,860 --> 00:07:42,840
I can't believe it.
Falling for a senior's pickup line.

113
00:07:43,160 --> 00:07:45,904
Beautiful women have a good eye for men.
Well then,

114
00:07:45,954 --> 00:07:48,420
I'm leaving the Porsche to you.

115
00:07:49,840 --> 00:07:51,100
Leave it to me!

116
00:07:51,560 --> 00:07:52,680
Aaaaaah!

117
00:07:53,700 --> 00:07:55,560
Well then, shall we go?

118
00:07:57,680 --> 00:07:58,220
Here we go.

119
00:08:01,220 --> 00:08:02,340
S-senpai!

120
00:08:05,320 --> 00:08:07,260
Phew, honestly.

121
00:08:16,300 --> 00:08:16,820
It's turning!

122
00:08:18,280 --> 00:08:21,000
How mean.

123
00:08:25,160 --> 00:08:26,120
Yes!

124
00:08:41,200 --> 00:08:42,440
What's your name?

125
00:08:43,000 --> 00:08:43,900
It's Kyoko.

126
00:08:43,900 --> 00:08:45,980
What are your hobbies?

127
00:08:46,420 --> 00:08:49,140
My job is researching cooking,

128
00:08:49,520 --> 00:08:52,040
but I also teach flower arranging,
tea ceremony, and martial arts.

129
00:08:52,800 --> 00:08:56,500
And I love cars so much that I race them.

130
00:08:56,500 --> 00:08:58,060
You have quite a few hobbies, don't you?

131
00:08:58,060 --> 00:09:00,480
I love cars too, you know.

132
00:09:00,480 --> 00:09:01,680
Looks like we'd get along.

133
00:09:03,900 --> 00:09:05,060
Is that so?

134
00:09:05,060 --> 00:09:06,720
Ryotsu-san, what are your hobbies?

135
00:09:06,940 --> 00:09:09,040
Eating food, of course.

136
00:09:09,860 --> 00:09:13,280
How do you know my name?

137
00:09:14,520 --> 00:09:16,720
From the Kameari Kōen-mae police box,

138
00:09:16,720 --> 00:09:19,080
there's no one who doesn't
know Kankichi Ryotsu-san

139
00:09:19,080 --> 00:09:20,820
in all of Tokyo.

140
00:09:22,140 --> 00:09:25,800
Is that so? I'm that famous? You flatter me.

141
00:09:26,460 --> 00:09:29,408
But I feel like we've met somewhere before,

142
00:09:29,458 --> 00:09:32,280
you know. You look like someone close to me.

143
00:09:33,280 --> 00:09:35,480
This is our first time meeting, isn't it?

144
00:09:36,980 --> 00:09:38,440
That ring!

145
00:09:39,600 --> 00:09:41,540
Actually, I'm married.

146
00:09:41,740 --> 00:09:44,340
I don't mind that at all.

147
00:09:44,880 --> 00:09:47,840
I've always been good at taking
things that belong to others.

148
00:09:48,300 --> 00:09:50,540
Her husband's probably some ugly guy, right?

149
00:09:52,040 --> 00:09:56,540
Hey, he must be, for sure!
What's his face like?

150
00:09:57,360 --> 00:10:04,300
His bangs are sharp and his eyes are dashing.
Those bangs are well kept, so dashing!

151
00:10:04,300 --> 00:10:08,340
With a magnificent beard...
well, yes, indeed.

152
00:10:09,640 --> 00:10:13,660
His hair is a bowl-cut style, like a kappa's head.
Bowl cut!

153
00:10:18,920 --> 00:10:20,140
What's the matter?

154
00:10:20,460 --> 00:10:22,740
No, no, it's nothing.

155
00:10:23,780 --> 00:10:27,080
That old bastard can't
possibly be her husband.

156
00:10:27,080 --> 00:10:28,840
I'm losing my mind here.

157
00:10:28,840 --> 00:10:31,040
Imagining a face like that...

158
00:10:32,380 --> 00:10:33,620
Is it already this late?

159
00:10:34,300 --> 00:10:36,980
Ryotsu-san, I'll be taking my leave now.

160
00:10:36,980 --> 00:10:39,080
I see... I see.

161
00:10:39,600 --> 00:10:41,460
Well, I'll take care of the bill here.

162
00:10:41,460 --> 00:10:44,280
Thank you for the meal. Well then.

163
00:10:44,280 --> 00:10:47,120
Do you think I could see you again?

164
00:10:48,920 --> 00:10:52,440
Next time, I'll be the one to invite you.
Farewell.

165
00:10:54,700 --> 00:10:56,040
Yes!

166
00:10:56,980 --> 00:10:59,140
She looks refined, doesn't she?
Such a stunning beauty!

167
00:11:00,120 --> 00:11:03,300
Right? Apparently she's
a cooking researcher.

168
00:11:03,960 --> 00:11:06,622
Her driving skills are top-notch too,

169
00:11:06,672 --> 00:11:08,480
and her style was outstanding.

170
00:11:09,940 --> 00:11:12,840
At last,
I can see the red string of fate for me too.

171
00:11:12,840 --> 00:11:15,041
Pasted all over with...

172
00:11:15,091 --> 00:11:18,280
Dizzy and spinning even on the ceiling,

173
00:11:19,260 --> 00:11:20,920
Red string... don't tell me

174
00:11:20,920 --> 00:11:24,680
Goodbye to my long bachelor life!

175
00:11:24,680 --> 00:11:27,212
Wait a moment, senior,

176
00:11:27,262 --> 00:11:29,660
isn't she a married woman?

177
00:11:30,160 --> 00:11:34,160
That's right, Ryo-chan, stop it!
Trying to seduce a married woman!

178
00:11:34,160 --> 00:11:34,997
Shut up!

179
00:11:35,047 --> 00:11:39,660
The more obstacles there are,
the more the flames of love blaze up!

180
00:11:41,920 --> 00:11:43,000
Maria

181
00:11:44,840 --> 00:11:48,140
My heart is burning with
the flames of jealousy.

182
00:11:49,440 --> 00:11:50,460
Your Majesty.

183
00:11:50,460 --> 00:11:53,600
Even with me here,
you're still trying so hard?

184
00:11:53,600 --> 00:11:56,460
Calm down, Maria.

185
00:11:57,980 --> 00:12:00,140
Then please give up on the married woman.

186
00:12:00,140 --> 00:12:03,060
Listen carefully, you're a man.

187
00:12:03,060 --> 00:12:05,160
You can't marry me.

188
00:12:05,160 --> 00:12:08,260
But that lady is married,
though she's still a woman.

189
00:12:09,660 --> 00:12:10,740
You could marry her.

190
00:12:10,740 --> 00:12:12,220
Ryo-sama, that's cruel!

191
00:12:12,360 --> 00:12:15,060
When I adore you with
my whole heart like this!

192
00:12:17,540 --> 00:12:20,200
Ryo-sama doesn't like Maria at all.

193
00:12:28,640 --> 00:12:30,040
What? What's going on?

194
00:12:31,000 --> 00:12:35,600
Why is my mother in a picture with Ryo-sama?

195
00:12:35,780 --> 00:12:36,560
What?

196
00:12:36,560 --> 00:12:40,420
So this beauty is Maria's mother?

197
00:12:53,000 --> 00:12:57,090
I thought I'd seen that
face somewhere before,

198
00:12:57,140 --> 00:12:59,900
but I never imagined she was Maria's mother.

199
00:12:59,900 --> 00:13:01,980
It's a small world, isn't it.

200
00:13:02,440 --> 00:13:06,520
But she looks awfully young
to be Maria-chan's mother.

201
00:13:06,520 --> 00:13:08,480
I'm only thirty-six.

202
00:13:09,200 --> 00:13:11,460
So if she's Maria's mother,

203
00:13:12,040 --> 00:13:14,580
that bookshelf-faced old man is her husband?

204
00:13:16,880 --> 00:13:19,120
Maria, how old are you now?

205
00:13:19,120 --> 00:13:20,240
I'm twenty.

206
00:13:21,040 --> 00:13:21,840
That means...

207
00:13:23,740 --> 00:13:26,100
she had you when she was sixteen?

208
00:13:26,600 --> 00:13:27,000
Yes.

209
00:13:27,000 --> 00:13:27,200
Yes.

210
00:13:29,400 --> 00:13:32,560
At sixteen, she'd just
graduated from junior high school.

211
00:13:33,060 --> 00:13:33,420
Yes.

212
00:13:33,700 --> 00:13:35,740
Unbelievable! That damn old man,

213
00:13:35,790 --> 00:13:37,880
he's a total lecher, just like he looks!

214
00:13:38,540 --> 00:13:40,380
Hey, kid, marry me!

215
00:13:40,660 --> 00:13:41,140
Eek!

216
00:13:42,640 --> 00:13:45,120
Isn't that a crime, one step away?

217
00:13:45,620 --> 00:13:47,400
My father didn't actually court her.

218
00:13:47,980 --> 00:13:50,500
It was my mother who fell
madly in love with my father.

219
00:13:50,900 --> 00:13:52,280
Whoa! What did you say?

220
00:13:52,580 --> 00:13:53,900
It was your mother who did.

221
00:13:57,000 --> 00:13:58,159
Unbelievable.

222
00:13:58,209 --> 00:14:02,240
What's so great about that
octopus-dancing swordsman?

223
00:14:02,700 --> 00:14:04,760
They had a fateful encounter.

224
00:14:05,920 --> 00:14:07,528
My mother,
the heiress of a gourmet conglomerate,

225
00:14:07,578 --> 00:14:12,000
was born to Imada Denmon's
father and a dancer mother.

226
00:14:12,540 --> 00:14:13,420
Good day.

227
00:14:13,620 --> 00:14:14,420
Good day.

228
00:14:15,300 --> 00:14:18,880
She was raised with great care,
like a doll kept in a box.

229
00:14:19,420 --> 00:14:22,453
One day, out of curiosity,
she went outside alone,

230
00:14:22,503 --> 00:14:25,000
and got caught up with some bad guys.

231
00:14:27,000 --> 00:14:29,040
Then my father, who was out training,
happened to pass by.

232
00:14:29,040 --> 00:14:30,940
Hey, cutie.

233
00:14:31,440 --> 00:14:32,740
Come hang out with us.

234
00:14:32,740 --> 00:14:34,640
What are you doing! Stop it!

235
00:14:35,000 --> 00:14:36,640
That face is irresistible.

236
00:14:36,640 --> 00:14:37,160
Stop it!

237
00:14:42,580 --> 00:14:44,600
It all happened in an instant.

238
00:14:45,040 --> 00:14:47,280
He took down every last thug in a flash.

239
00:14:48,540 --> 00:14:49,600
My mother's heart

240
00:14:49,600 --> 00:14:52,940
must have seemed like a prince riding
in on a white horse to rescue her.

241
00:14:54,040 --> 00:14:56,800
So she fell for him
completely at first sight.

242
00:14:56,800 --> 00:15:00,720
It's the kind of illusion sheltered
young ladies tend to fall for.

243
00:15:00,720 --> 00:15:04,040
But her parents must have opposed it, too.

244
00:15:04,880 --> 00:15:06,860
But my mother's resolve was firm.

245
00:15:07,420 --> 00:15:10,620
Father boarded a plane
to New York for training,

246
00:15:10,620 --> 00:15:13,120
and the two of them eloped.

247
00:15:14,320 --> 00:15:16,900
And that's where I was born, in New York.

248
00:15:16,900 --> 00:15:20,740
I heard that because of that,
her parents eventually forgave them.

249
00:15:21,320 --> 00:15:22,600
Well, that's good, then.

250
00:15:22,940 --> 00:15:24,500
That's so dramatic, Senior.

251
00:15:24,740 --> 00:15:26,260
What's so dramatic about it?

252
00:15:26,460 --> 00:15:29,200
That old fool Hontaro is just deceiving her.

253
00:15:29,540 --> 00:15:31,620
I'll wake her up myself.

254
00:15:31,920 --> 00:15:33,943
Still, she's beautiful even now,

255
00:15:33,993 --> 00:15:36,620
she must have been stunning back then.

256
00:15:37,280 --> 00:15:38,720
Damn you, Hontaro!

257
00:15:49,480 --> 00:15:51,100
Ai-chan, how have you been?

258
00:15:53,300 --> 00:15:55,980
Yes, you look even more
beautiful in the daytime.

259
00:15:57,140 --> 00:15:59,420
Ryo-san,
thank you for the meal this morning.

260
00:15:59,420 --> 00:16:02,134
Oh my, I never expected to see you again,

261
00:16:02,184 --> 00:16:03,740
Well, please, come right in.

262
00:16:03,740 --> 00:16:07,460
Ryo-sama! Mother, that's cruel!

263
00:16:07,460 --> 00:16:11,320
How could you go on a date with
him when you know I love Ryo-sama?

264
00:16:12,200 --> 00:16:13,860
Ai-chan, please forgive me.

265
00:16:13,860 --> 00:16:18,180
I only wanted to know what
kind of man Ai fell for.

266
00:16:18,180 --> 00:16:19,520
Is that so?

267
00:16:19,940 --> 00:16:23,140
So, how did Ryotsu appear to you, Mother?

268
00:16:23,400 --> 00:16:25,738
As unique as my darling,

269
00:16:25,788 --> 00:16:27,700
and a good match for Ai.

270
00:16:27,700 --> 00:16:30,760
Wow, I'm so happy! As expected of Mom.

271
00:16:31,300 --> 00:16:32,614
I came to visit because

272
00:16:32,664 --> 00:16:37,060
I wanted to invite Mr.
Ryotsu over for dinner.

273
00:16:37,060 --> 00:16:37,900
Really?

274
00:16:38,380 --> 00:16:41,640
If you like,
all of you please join us as well.

275
00:16:41,640 --> 00:16:42,760
Wow, how wonderful!

276
00:16:42,760 --> 00:16:43,520
Don't mind if we do.

277
00:16:45,220 --> 00:16:47,433
I'm far better-looking than
that dimwit of a father,

278
00:16:47,483 --> 00:16:50,200
so this is my chance to
show her what a catch I am.

279
00:16:55,520 --> 00:16:57,760
Welcome, everyone. Please, come in.

280
00:16:58,060 --> 00:16:58,460
Thank you.

281
00:17:02,260 --> 00:17:03,060
Hey!

282
00:17:04,160 --> 00:17:06,280
Line up your shoes properly.

283
00:17:09,240 --> 00:17:11,780
Even with white lines painted on the floor,
she's so meticulous.

284
00:17:12,760 --> 00:17:15,180
Mother's only flaw is that she's
a little too fond of cleanliness.

285
00:17:15,740 --> 00:17:17,660
If she's beautiful, I'll forgive anything.

286
00:17:17,660 --> 00:17:19,080
Aaaaah!

287
00:17:20,040 --> 00:17:22,080
What's wrong, Mother?

288
00:17:22,620 --> 00:17:23,400
In the hallway...

289
00:17:27,020 --> 00:17:29,540
A cat must have snuck into the house.

290
00:17:29,540 --> 00:17:31,140
Darling.

291
00:17:31,760 --> 00:17:34,240
Yes, yes, honey, I'm home.

292
00:17:34,240 --> 00:17:35,460
Ryotsu...

293
00:17:35,460 --> 00:17:36,800
Ryotsu?

294
00:17:39,560 --> 00:17:42,120
"Darling"?
Cut it out, at your age, honestly!

295
00:17:42,880 --> 00:17:44,440
Why are you here?!

296
00:17:44,820 --> 00:17:46,240
I invited him.

297
00:17:46,900 --> 00:17:49,498
Anyway, there are cat paw
prints all over the hallway.

298
00:17:49,548 --> 00:17:51,020
Clean it up right away.

299
00:17:51,540 --> 00:17:53,620
Yes, yes, honey. Right away.

300
00:17:54,860 --> 00:17:57,820
Whoa! H-hey! That's my job!

301
00:17:58,480 --> 00:18:01,322
I'm such a clean freak,
so when I see something dirty,

302
00:18:01,372 --> 00:18:03,060
I just have to clean it up.

303
00:18:03,480 --> 00:18:06,240
There are more over here and
on the shoji over there too.

304
00:18:07,800 --> 00:18:09,280
You said it was my job!

305
00:18:09,360 --> 00:18:10,260
Japan is dirty too.

306
00:18:10,440 --> 00:18:11,220
Hey, cut it out!

307
00:18:11,520 --> 00:18:12,660
Here we go, twist, twist, twist.

308
00:18:12,700 --> 00:18:13,700
Stop it, don't blow!

309
00:18:13,920 --> 00:18:14,500
Hoi hoi.

310
00:18:14,560 --> 00:18:15,680
I told you to stop!

311
00:18:16,020 --> 00:18:16,860
Do it for me!

312
00:18:16,860 --> 00:18:17,340
I'll do it!

313
00:18:17,640 --> 00:18:18,840
Wow, how wonderful!

314
00:18:19,220 --> 00:18:22,140
I had no idea Mr. Ryotsu
was such a clean freak.

315
00:18:23,020 --> 00:18:25,000
Darling,
you should follow suit too, you know.

316
00:18:25,560 --> 00:18:26,640
Uh-huh, uh-huh.

317
00:18:27,040 --> 00:18:30,376
Yes! From now on, I'll show everyone

318
00:18:30,426 --> 00:18:32,340
just how much more of a man I am.

319
00:18:32,760 --> 00:18:33,560
Hey, Ryotsu!

320
00:18:33,940 --> 00:18:35,640
Lady Ruki, you've been hogging her!

321
00:18:36,020 --> 00:18:38,280
You're far too good for Honey.

322
00:18:38,280 --> 00:18:40,380
She's much better suited to me.

323
00:18:40,380 --> 00:18:41,300
What did you say?

324
00:18:41,300 --> 00:18:43,940
Darling, what are you whispering about?

325
00:18:44,640 --> 00:18:46,660
Honey, it's nothing.

326
00:18:47,100 --> 00:18:49,640
I won't let you get away with
doing whatever you please anymore.

327
00:18:55,040 --> 00:18:56,660
This way, please.

328
00:19:01,100 --> 00:19:02,460
Such a spacious Japanese-style room,

329
00:19:04,080 --> 00:19:05,800
what a luxurious tatami room.

330
00:19:06,720 --> 00:19:10,021
Y-you went and matched
everything up in pairs,

331
00:19:10,071 --> 00:19:13,200
like a couple of newlyweds,
for crying out loud.

332
00:19:13,440 --> 00:19:14,220
Nice and warm, isn't it.

333
00:19:15,020 --> 00:19:16,020
Don't touch that, hey!

334
00:19:16,360 --> 00:19:19,940
Old geezer like you, don't use couple's mugs.
It's disgusting.

335
00:19:20,420 --> 00:19:21,500
Mind your own business.

336
00:19:22,940 --> 00:19:24,240
What's wrong, Honey?

337
00:19:24,400 --> 00:19:27,560
Look over there. Could it be
from the earthquake the other day?

338
00:19:27,680 --> 00:19:30,630
That garden stone has shifted
about one centimeter to the right.

339
00:19:30,680 --> 00:19:32,180
Would you fix it?

340
00:19:33,460 --> 00:19:34,180
Leave it to me.

341
00:19:38,160 --> 00:19:40,440
Maria, is it all right to just stay quiet?

342
00:19:40,700 --> 00:19:43,700
Ryo-chan still hasn't given up on your mother,
you know.

343
00:19:43,700 --> 00:19:46,800
Father and Mother are such a perfect match.

344
00:19:46,800 --> 00:19:49,440
No need to worry,
no matter what Ryo-sama does.

345
00:19:53,100 --> 00:19:55,500
You can't handle this. Let me take over.

346
00:19:55,500 --> 00:19:58,040
Shut up, this is nothing!

347
00:19:58,040 --> 00:19:58,800
Run away!

348
00:20:02,240 --> 00:20:06,260
I told you! Your training and
mine are completely different!

349
00:20:16,060 --> 00:20:19,720
You two are both old enough to
know better than to be reckless.

350
00:20:20,000 --> 00:20:20,400
Yes.

351
00:20:22,660 --> 00:20:24,840
Dinner is ready.

352
00:20:25,740 --> 00:20:27,100
Wow, that looks delicious!

353
00:20:31,180 --> 00:20:33,160
As expected from a cooking expert.

354
00:20:33,160 --> 00:20:36,280
It's my own original creation,
a fusion of Japanese and Western cuisine.

355
00:20:36,280 --> 00:20:39,500
Maria, that's enough, I'm going to dig in.

356
00:20:39,500 --> 00:20:40,720
Hey, wait!

357
00:20:41,220 --> 00:20:45,140
Oh my, I've never had such
delicious home-cooked food in my life!

358
00:20:46,800 --> 00:20:49,640
I'm so glad to hear you say that.

359
00:20:51,120 --> 00:20:54,080
I get to eat that three times a day.

360
00:20:54,080 --> 00:20:55,600
Jealous, aren't you, Ryotsu?

361
00:20:55,600 --> 00:20:57,600
It's not about the number of times, look.

362
00:20:58,040 --> 00:20:59,740
I've already eaten this much!

363
00:21:00,200 --> 00:21:01,660
As if I'd lose to you!

364
00:21:03,680 --> 00:21:04,640
Damn it, I'm wrecking this place!

365
00:21:05,000 --> 00:21:06,340
Hey, hey, Ryo-chan!

366
00:21:09,540 --> 00:21:13,300
Thank you for the meal!
Food made with love is the best!

367
00:21:14,400 --> 00:21:16,000
I ate more!

368
00:21:16,560 --> 00:21:17,880
Obviously it was me!

369
00:21:18,320 --> 00:21:18,920
What did you say?!

370
00:21:19,440 --> 00:21:22,760
My, I'm so glad you're
enjoying it that much.

371
00:21:23,040 --> 00:21:25,240
There's still plenty more food prepared.

372
00:21:28,680 --> 00:21:31,080
There's still more? I'm already

373
00:21:31,080 --> 00:21:34,580
Please, if it's a dish filled with big brother's love,
I'll eat plenty, Yone.

374
00:21:34,580 --> 00:21:37,480
No, even I can still eat more!

375
00:21:37,480 --> 00:21:41,122
What's wrong?

376
00:21:41,172 --> 00:21:43,480
Ai-chan

377
00:21:43,480 --> 00:21:45,960
Just now, someone sneaked into the garden!

378
00:21:46,300 --> 00:21:47,440
Isn't it a thief?

379
00:21:47,780 --> 00:21:48,100
What?

380
00:21:48,540 --> 00:21:50,020
Right, I'll catch him!

381
00:21:50,020 --> 00:21:51,640
No, I'll catch him!

382
00:21:52,500 --> 00:21:54,544
Leave the thief to the darlings,

383
00:21:54,594 --> 00:21:56,540
and let's keep eating.

384
00:21:58,040 --> 00:21:58,680
Hey, you!

385
00:21:58,760 --> 00:22:00,100
Here he comes!

386
00:22:06,320 --> 00:22:09,357
Damn, I was going to show off...

387
00:22:09,407 --> 00:22:11,260
This guy's pretty tough.

388
00:22:21,060 --> 00:22:24,220
Damn it, now I'll show you the secret
technique of the Bookshelf Sword!

389
00:22:24,220 --> 00:22:25,580
Haaah!

390
00:22:25,580 --> 00:22:28,200
It's Buffy's Miya-chan and Myu-chan!

391
00:22:28,840 --> 00:22:29,500
Opening!

392
00:22:34,120 --> 00:22:37,120
I'm wearing protectors,
just in case something like this happened.

393
00:22:37,560 --> 00:22:39,020
You're a martial arts pro

394
00:22:44,260 --> 00:22:45,420
Doesn't work at all.

395
00:22:45,420 --> 00:22:48,260
Doesn't hurt or itch one bit.

396
00:22:52,740 --> 00:22:55,400
Guess I'll grab some valuables right away.

397
00:22:55,800 --> 00:22:57,380
Oh no, they're coming inside!

398
00:23:01,980 --> 00:23:03,460
I can't forgive this.

399
00:23:04,880 --> 00:23:06,320
Exa-!

400
00:23:07,640 --> 00:23:08,980
Where's the bank?

401
00:23:08,980 --> 00:23:09,380
Hey, wait a minute.

402
00:23:19,040 --> 00:23:20,720
O-only one blow!

403
00:23:21,140 --> 00:23:23,340
I trained him myself, mind you,

404
00:23:23,390 --> 00:23:25,640
but he's become stronger than me.

405
00:23:26,440 --> 00:23:27,760
You two!

406
00:23:38,480 --> 00:23:40,720
Make sure you clean it properly. Understand?

407
00:23:41,720 --> 00:23:43,400
Yes. Sorry, ma'am.

408
00:23:44,260 --> 00:23:47,960
How do you put up with
such a terrifying honey?

409
00:23:48,260 --> 00:23:50,390
Well, I do love her.

410
00:23:50,440 --> 00:23:52,620
I'm done with marriage for now.

411
00:23:52,700 --> 00:23:54,620
You there! Stop laughing like idiots!

412
00:23:55,380 --> 00:23:56,440
Yes, yes, yes!

413
00:23:57,220 --> 00:23:58,300
Yes, yes, yes!

414
00:23:59,720 --> 00:24:00,480
Me and...

415
00:24:04,180 --> 00:24:05,920
What's wrong? Why the long face?

416
00:24:06,420 --> 00:24:09,340
That's not like you, Kotone-chan. Cheer up!

417
00:24:10,080 --> 00:24:12,614
Right, if Hanayashiki's
satellite gets infected,

418
00:24:12,664 --> 00:24:14,160
let's ride it together.

419
00:24:14,420 --> 00:24:17,580
Being first in line.
It's a promise, definitely!

420
00:24:18,260 --> 00:24:21,480
Next time:
"Asakusa First Love Story." See you then.

421
00:24:48,260 --> 00:24:59,180
I want to ride a motorbike,
I want to be freer than a bird.

422
00:24:59,960 --> 00:25:07,060
At the speed of a kaleidoscope,
a lady's dreams keep changing.

423
00:25:08,840 --> 00:25:15,100
Heart of love, sorry, I lost.

424
00:25:15,100 --> 00:25:22,200
The dazzling brilliance of
living a panoramic future.

425
00:25:23,460 --> 00:25:26,534
You understand, right?

426
00:25:26,584 --> 00:25:30,100
Sorry, wait for me.

